    },
    {
      "contract": "Preflight write probe has no authority to carry a real hold",
      "location": "internal/api/install_parsed_manifest.go:preflightSupervisorIntentWrite",
      "observation": "With a nonzero hold the helper clones the desired whole intent, clears hold only on that private probe, and passes the probe to WriteSupervisorIntent at the temporary path. The desired intent remains held for real commit; existing master write owner preserves current on-disk hold.",
      "test": "TestInstallPreflightPreservesBackendRunHold is byte-identical, checks desired equality/held error, original file bytes and probe/lock absence."
    },
    {
      "contract": "Real call sites and callbacks retained",
      "location": "internal/api/install_parsed_manifest.go and internal/api/install.go",
      "observation": "Observed prior read and regular read paths still converge on the same merge owner. Projected-row callback is unchanged. Legacy install preflight and observed invocation-preflight remain distinct as before; SID patch does not alter merge/commit/rollback callbacks. API schedulerStatusForOwnPort remains defaultSchedulerStatusForOwnPort→scheduler.New().Status."
    },
    {
      "contract": "Native principal projection reaches the Go port owner gate",
      "location": "scheduler_com_windows.go:Get-OwnerSID/list/status → scheduler_windows.go:Status/ListContext → api/install.go:statusOwnedByCurrentUser",
      "observation": "Status/List resolve a principal to canonical SID before TaskStatus; unknown/empty projection fails closed without a partial public result. Platform scheduler/current migration owner now retains user.Current().Uid. Windows API compares the resolved Owner with current.Uid, retaining former non-Windows account projection. There is no short-name/domain-stripping fallback on this Windows chain."
    },
    {
      "contract": "Migration inventory and RunOwned use the same owner identity",
      "location": "entrypoint_migration_windows.go and scheduler_com_windows.go:Test-OwnedDefinition",
      "observation": "Migration comparisons consume TaskStatus.Owner from List, which is now SID-based; XML export remains raw XML and does not substitute its raw owner string into the comparison. RunOwned still resolves both XML and native principal via the same resolver; resolver failure remains guarded mismatch, without Run effect."
    },
    {
      "contract": "Test boundary honesty",
      "location": "scheduler_owner_sid_windows_test.go and api/scheduler_owner_sid_windows_test.go",
      "observation": "PowerShell fixture replaces exactly the COM service constructor and account-name lookup; controlled ScriptMethod Run records only a marker, never a native task run. Literal SecurityIdentifier parsing/production validation/error projection stay real. API test fixes private empty state, PID/image/Status callbacks and asserts exactly one actual port-decision Status query. Native account/domain resolution and Scheduler rights/effects are not thereby qualified."
    },
    {
      "contract": "Existing last-result semantics preserved",
      "location": "scheduler_last_result_windows_test.go",
      "observation": "Only fixture owner strings/expected platform owner change to SID literals. Missing/null/malformed LastTaskResult classifications, numeric runtime state and hidden-task/recovery overlays remain unchanged."
